      "claim": "The commander exercised effective command and control over MLC troops, satisfying the first element of Article 28(a).",
      "reasoning": "Article 28(a) requires that a military commander or a person effectively acting as one have \"effective command and control\" over the forces whose crimes are at issue. The Trial Chamber’s finding that the commander acted as a military commander with effective control directly meets this statutory requirement.",
